{
  "schema": "praxis.requirement-catalog/1",
  "catalogId": "CAT-CAUSA-INVESTIGATION",
  "idPattern": "^INV-\\d{3}$",
  "status": "ratified",
  "description": "PROPOSED SUCCESSOR (ODR-R10-02) of the ratified CAT-CAUSA-INVESTIGATION (sha256 19a03668..., INV-001..038): distinct screens and routes for the list, start and workspace (SA-04), and INV-039..044 for application structure (adversarial audit R4). Nothing ratified is changed except the workspace route; every new entry is sourced from an existing approved requirement. Component kinds are those Dokimos judges (region, link, display): Dokimos refuses list, navigation and status, so the audit draft's kinds are replaced. Behaviour the catalog cannot express (destinations activating, sections showing content, seven save states driven) is judged by the governed journeys J1-J3. Field-level decomposition of the authoritative Causa investigation requirements: creation and workspace (SCREEN-CONTRACTS S01, S02, S04, S05; REQUIREMENTS R1-R3, R10; CAUSA-UI-EXPERIENCE UI-006; CAUSA-PERSISTENCE PERSIST-007, PERSIST-021, PERSIST-030), INV-001..INV-018; and investigation content, the Rehearsal 9 content gaps and the answers to the catalog's open questions (OD-INDY-19..21, OD-INDY-23), INV-019..INV-038. Drafted by an agent; ratified by the owner.",
